e sugar|white sugar]]\n* 1 cup (150 g) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] cake emulsifier\n* 50 g grated [[Cookbook:Orange|orange]]\n* 2½ cups (375 g) [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n\n=== Garnishing ===\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Whipped Cream|whipped cream]]\n* 10 pieces [[Cookbook:Orange|oranges]]\n* 100 g [[Cookbook:Strawberry|strawberry]], halved\n* 75 g [[Cookbook:Kiwifruit|kiwifruit]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Combine egg yolks, butter, sugar, and cake emulsifier in an electric mixer. [[Cookbook:Whipping|Whip]] until light and expanded.\n# Combine the flour, baking soda, and grated orange. [[Cookbook:Folding|Fold]] into the egg yolk mixture.\n# Grease a [[Cookbook:Baking Pan|baking pan]] with butter.\n# Transfer the batter to the prepared baking pan. [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 20 minutes at 360°F (185°C) until an inserted [[Cookbook:Skewer|skewer]] comes out clean.\n# Let cake cool, and transfer to a serving plate.\n# Spread all sides of cake with the whipped cream.\n# Garnish with orange, strawberry and kiwifruit, and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for cake]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Holiday recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg yolk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whipped cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using orange]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using strawberry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using kiwifruit]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Fruit Cake","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"8 egg yolks","sourceText":"8 egg yolks","amountText":"8 egg yolks","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cups (300 g) white sugar","sourceText":"2 cups (300 g) white sugar","amountText":"2 cups (300 g) white sugar","amount":nu